   "Date taken from the print code EIGI-00.10-HB next to the reference number in the footer (no other date printed). Exposure daylight, 1/50 s; process E-6/CR-56; densitometry Fuji FAD-30S (Status A). x axis of curves is log H in lux-seconds as printed. RMS granularity 8: diffuse, 48 um aperture, sample density 1.0 above minimum density (page 5).",
   "curves: the green curve (dash-dot) is above the red one from the plateau (D 3.42 against 3.30 for red, 3.34 for blue) to log H -1.5 (D 1.9), where it disappears under the red curve; the blue curve (dashed navy) leaves the red curve at the plateau, rejoins it at log H -2.15 (D 3.0) and is hidden under it from there on. Where g and b are hidden they are traced on the red curve's ink (g about +0.02, b about +0.01 in the hints; the trace sees the same line), so g and b equal r below log H -1.5. The three curves end at log H 0.83 (D-min plateau 0.09 for the red curve).",
   "sensitivity: y is relative log sensitivity as printed (sensitivity = reciprocal of the exposure in J/cm2 giving 1.0 above D-min). Curves are drawn only from about -0.85 (blue, 389-501 nm), -0.6 (green, 475-597 nm) and -0.55 (red, 571-671 nm) up to their peaks; the end drops are near vertical so the last 1-2 nm are approximated.",
   "dyes: spectral diffuse density of the separated dyes (max 1.0), curves 387-717 nm; coloured ink, traced per colour. Magenta and cyan cross near 420 nm (D 0.2) and 588 nm (D 0.5); yellow and magenta near 490 nm (0.45); yellow and cyan near 518 nm (0.13). Yellow runs along the base (0.03-0.01) beyond 580 nm."
